Gap 2: interactive programs (do first, it's small)

The current model is "type a line, compile it, run it, return to prompt." A program is different: it starts, it keeps running, it polls input, it draws, it exits. The only thing missing is non-blocking input and a main convention. Both are trivial.

```c
// non-blocking: push 1 if a scancode is waiting, 0 otherwise
HELPER void h_keyq(void) {
    uint8_t status; __asm__ volatile("inb $0x64, %0" : "=a"(status));
    g_sp[0] = (Rat){(status & 1) ? 1 : 0, 1}; g_sp++;
}
// blocking: wait for a scancode and push it
HELPER void h_key(void) {
    while (1) {
        uint8_t status; __asm__ volatile("inb $0x64, %0" : "=a"(status));
        if (status & 1) {
            uint8_t sc; __asm__ volatile("inb $0x60, %0" : "=a"(sc));
            g_sp[0] = (Rat){(int64_t)sc, 1}; g_sp++;
            return;
        }
    }
}
```

